A. pass rules: probability that a build passes, in basis points
   q = chance one seed is outside the band; rule SR1 all, SR2 at least ceil(9n/10) inside
   n   q      SR1(all)  SR2(9 in 10)
   10    1%     9044     9957
   10    2%     8171     9838
   10    5%     5987     9139
   10   20%     1074     3758
   10   30%      282     1493
   10   50%       10      107
   50    1%     6050    10000
   50    2%     3642     9995
   50    5%      769     9622
   50   20%        0      480
   50   30%        0        7
   50   50%        0        0
   false fail = 10000 - pass at the small q; power = 10000 - pass at the large q

B. a new seed outside the envelope of m exchangeable seeds: 2/(m+1)
  m=3 exact: 12/24 = 5000 bp (2/(m+1) = 5000 bp)
  m=5 exact: 240/720 = 3333 bp (2/(m+1) = 3333 bp)
  m=7 exact: 10080/40320 = 2500 bp (2/(m+1) = 2500 bp)
  m=10 formula: 1818 bp
  m=40 formula: 488 bp
  m=50 formula: 392 bp

C. headroom and rounding of the band-setting rule on 10 NEW seeds, i.e. what a hold-out gives (trials of 2000)
   band = [min - h*range, max + h*range] of m setting seeds, rounded outward to two significant digits
   (against REF's seeds the gate seeds are among the setting seeds, so the gate shows a change of the code)
   rows: P(all 10 gate seeds inside), P(at least 9 of 10 inside), in basis points
